  "name": "Low-level battleground players are lifted to their bracket top while inside",
  "contract": "A level 12 Human Warrior and a level 12 Human class 12 who enter a Warsong Gulch of the 10-29 bracket get base health and defensive gear catch-up applied directly to maximum health (UNIT_MOD_HEALTH) and armor (UNIT_MOD_ARMOR): the base difference between the level 29 and level 12 rows of player_class_stats and player_race_stats in base health plus Stamina health plus the green-gear Health budget difference (365 - 158 = 207 with no Stamina gear equipped), leaving Stamina and every other primary stat untouched. Warrior Stamina +0 and maximum health +666 (239 base health + 22 Stamina x 10 + 207 gear health); class 12 Stamina +0 and maximum health +601 (254 base health + 14 Stamina x 10 + 207 gear health). Strength, Agility, Intellect, Spirit and mana are not lifted and are not asserted here; the output scaling scenario checks that they stay put. A level 29 Orc Warrior gets nothing; a second one completes the faction pairing for the class 12 player. Leveling to 13 inside recomputes both lifts instead of stacking them: Stamina rises only by the natural level 13 gain (+1) while maximum health stands at the level 29 lifted value (+657 = 459 base + 198 gear health above the pre-entry level 12 baseline) and current health stays at 100%. Leaving through the leave packet or by teleport removes both lifts and clamps health to the restored maximum.",
